  "notes_for_editor": "Newspapers not searched successfully (Chronicling America query timed out). Disagreements recorded in text: when the light was first proposed (NRHP 1851, LighthouseFriends 1854); appropriation (LF June 1860, museum 1871); focal height (Putnam 196 ft, LF 198 ft); replica 1948 (NRHP) vs 1949 (LF); storm date (Bulletin/Putnam Dec 1913, LF Dec 1914; Wikipedia also says 1914, and its 200-ft wave estimate is not used). Date of the incandescent oil-vapor change is unknown (Bulletin index 1912-17 lists 'change in illuminant' p.95). Commissioner of Lighthouses FY1918 table lists keeper E. Wiborg of Trinidad Head under a rescue, but the OCR columns misalign (the '12 shipwrecked men' action belongs to Scotch Cap per the 1917 Bulletin), so it is not used; the Bulletin 1918 volume text lacks the p.40 Trinidad rescue entry. 1921 Bulletin lists 'fog signal established: Trinidad Head, bell, clockwork' which is unexplained and unused. USLHS roster ends 1969; LF says automated 1974 with Coast Guard residents to after 2000. Roster lines matched by roster tool output; Coast Guard crew entered with role 'crew'. The 1891-92 report volume covers two years; year of 14 November not fixed. 1969 four-plex (NRHP) vs triplex (LF). Checker: Pilot Rock height is 103 ft in the 1914 Bulletin OCR and 93 ft in LighthouseFriends's transcription; the page image was not viewed. Tour-only access wording reworded to match sources.",
